  "narrative": {
    "intro": "NAICS 336412, Aircraft Engine and Engine Parts Manufacturing, has $5.6B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Obligations are down 53.3% year over year. Award activity totals 9,719 awards with an average award size of $578K. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer with $5.5B in FY2026 to date. Historical annual obligations show variability: FY21 was $7.3B, FY22 was $11.1B, FY23 was $13.7B, FY24 was $8.4B, and FY25 was $12B. Top vendors in FY2026 to date include RTX CORPORATION with $1.7B, GENERAL ELECTRIC COMPANY with $1.3B, ROLLS-ROYCE CORPORATION with $903M, and a separate listing for GENERAL ELECTRIC COMPANY with $493M. Other FY2026 to date buyers include Department of Homeland Security with $103M and Department of Commerce with $7.1M. Current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is ongoing, and all figures reported here are contract obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have obligations changed recently?",
        "body": "NAICS 336412 obligations moved from $13.7B in FY23 down to $8.4B in FY24, then to $12B in FY25 and to $5.6B in FY26 to date. FY26 to date obligations are down 53.3% year over year. FY21 obligations were $7.3B and FY22 obligations were $11.1B. Current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is ongoing."
